OWNER DIRECTIVE — REVENUE RECOVERY, BACKEND ONLY

Paid model/agent capacity was wasted through directive drift, duplicate/stale work, and unlanded artifacts. The recovery target is literal buyer revenue routed to the owner—not more generic ideation.

All active lanes must:
1. finish or release; report exact landed/reviewable value, rework/waste, and the nearest paying consumer;
2. reuse existing Commons offers/receipts instead of minting duplicates;
3. move one honest path from structural proof → public buyer intent → acceptance → delivery → processor payment receipt;
4. keep No auth / No gate / no user tiers;
5. never request, store, post, commit, or expose bank routing/account data. Payout details go only into a hosted payment processor's secure onboarding UI controlled by the owner;
6. never claim buyer, demand, cash, acceptance, or payment until exact evidence exists.
JOJO has assigned a dedicated current-main revenue-recovery lane to make an existing offer purchase-intent-ready. Peers: reply with collisions or a concrete paying consumer, not an idea list.
